Description
Comprehensive documentation for the beast-micro-insurance repository, outlining its mission to replace predatory corporate insurance monopolies with community-funded smart contract risk pools, architecture details, and Google Cloud Run deployment instructions.

Core Code
Markdown
# BEAST Micro-Insurance (`beast-micro-insurance`)

`beast-micro-insurance` is a decentralized peer-to-peer mutual aid and risk pooling network under the New World Order Private Government framework. It provides a transparent, non-predatory alternative to corporate insurance monopolies, leveraging community-funded treasuries, peer assessor verification, and automated smart contract payouts.

---

## 🏗 Repository Architecture

```text
beast-micro-insurance/
├── contracts/               # Solidity smart contracts for mutual risk pools
│   └── MicroInsurancePool.sol # On-chain treasury and claim verification logic
├── backend/                 # Node.js Express API & PostgreSQL database integration
│   ├── src/                 # API routes, database connectors, and claim handlers
│   ├── db/                  # SQL schema definitions
│   └── Dockerfile           # Cloud Run container configuration
├── frontend/                # Next.js App Router portal for members and assessors
├── .github/workflows/       # CI/CD deployment pipeline to Google Cloud Run
└── README.md                # System documentation
🚀 Getting Started
1. Prerequisites
Node.js (>= 20.0.0)

PostgreSQL / Google Cloud SQL instance

MetaMask or compatible Web3 wallet

2. Run Backend Service
Bash
cd backend
npm install
npm run dev
3. Run Frontend Portal
Bash
cd frontend
npm install
npm run dev
🛡️ Core Principles
Mutual Aid Over Profit: Replaces bureaucratic corporate insurers with community-owned risk pools.

Transparent Verification: Peer-reviewed assessors validate claims directly on-chain without arbitrary denials.

Instant Smart Payouts: Funds are released programmatically via smart contracts the moment consensus is reached.
